course: dictionary
lesson: 9439
title: A word for everyone affected
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Stakeholder» is a long, stiff word, but the sentences around it give clues. «Stakeholders are everyone affected by a decision, including people and animals who are not in the room.» Affected means changed by something, so stakeholders are everyone a decision changes, even people who were never there.
explain: «Reading the case means finding the key facts and listing the stakeholders, everyone the choice affects.» The words after the comma explain the word. Try swapping in the meaning: «listing everyone the choice affects» still makes sense, so you have the right idea.
explain: Stakeholder is a formal word, often used in offices and exams. Context tells you its main meaning, but a dictionary helps with the other meanings, such as the business one and the old betting one.
fact: Stakeholder is a noun, and stakeholders is the plural.
fact: A stakeholder is a person or group who is affected by something, such as a plan or a business, so they care how it turns out.
fact: In business, a stakeholder can be someone who owns a share in a company or has money in it.
fact: In an old use, a stakeholder was a person who held the money people had bet until the winner was known.
fact: In school talk, pupils, parents and teachers are the stakeholders of a school.
exercise: «Stakeholders are everyone affected by a decision.» What are stakeholders? | Only the people in the room | People who make the decision alone | *Everyone affected by a decision | Shops near the school
exercise: «Reading the case means listing the stakeholders, everyone the choice affects.» What do the words after the comma tell you? | The case is a locked box | Only the teacher matters | The choice is a secret | *Who the stakeholders are: everyone the choice affects
exercise: Which group are the stakeholders of a school? | The buses only | The school dinners | *Pupils, parents and teachers | Only the building and the desks
test: Someone who owns a share in a company is called a what? | *A stakeholder | A postman | A stranger passing the building | A manager's secretary
test: In the old use, what did a stakeholder hold? | The winner's prize | A race horse | A map of the race | *The money people had bet, until the winner was known
exam: The phrase «key stakeholders» in a plan most likely means? | *The most important people affected by the plan | Spare keys for the school gates | Locks and keys for the office | The people who lost their keys
